 well and just get  it just get it everywhere you don't need  anything special if you want to put  something in the cavity you can but i  don't really think that that affects the  flavor too much if you want go ahead but  get it nice and salt and peppered  beautiful we've got it in there we want  to set our oven to 400 degrees which  we're at  we want that crispy skin the next most  important part about a juicy turkey is  your temperature set it to 155 and then  put it in the thickest part of the  breast  just like that  and then we're ready for the oven so  let's get it in there  okay so we'll go in the oven we'll set  our  we've got our  thermometer set to 155 and we'll see how  it turns out  okay so our turkey's been in the oven  and we're going to fast forward in time  here magic of tv it's been in for about  two hours it didn't take it very long  but during the process of cooking i've  been basting it with clarified butter or  ghee it's right here you can find that  on the baking aisle or you can make your  own um but it's just butter with the the  the liquids removed from it anyways i've  been basting it with that and that's  going to help that crispy skin so let's  get that turkey out of the oven and see  how it looks  i think it's going to be good  and would you look at that that looks  beautiful  another important thing i didn't mention  was is that we want to cook it to 155  and it came to that 155 looking  beautiful and if you look at it look at  the skin it's crispy i don't know if you  can hear that noise but it's perfect so  i'm so excited happy turkey cookie  cooking you can find all these things at  your local smiths thanks for watching  thanks for shopping and we'll see you  next time everybody bye-bye  there we go all right so thank you to  smith's food and drug for sponsoring  this segment for more information visit  smithfoodanddrug.com now i'm going to  send it over to a bunch of turkeys  this saturday
 

